## 4. Proof of Concept Design

### 4.1 Scaling for Available Compute

The full architecture — dual 4⁴ = 256 unit ensemble stacks with genuine physical parallelism across all 512 base units — requires hardware that does not currently exist as commodity infrastructure. Section 5.3 addresses this.

The proof of concept instantiates the same architectural principles at a reduced scale: dual 4² = 16 unit ensemble stacks, three levels of hierarchy (base units, four Level-1 ensembles of four units each, one Level-2 top ensemble), retaining the full structural relationships of the complete architecture.

The proof of concept is not a toy. It is a falsifiable demonstration of each architectural claim at a scale that can be evaluated on available infrastructure.

### 4.2 API-Isolated Parallel Deployment

The parallelism requirement — that the ensemble units run as genuinely isolated parallel processes, not as simulated parallelism on shared compute — is met in the proof of concept via API-isolated deployment. Each of the 16 base units (per layer) is deployed as a separate Hugging Face Space endpoint.

The input is broadcast to all 16 endpoints simultaneously via asynchronous HTTP calls. The responses are collected and concatenated by an orchestration layer as they arrive. The orchestration layer manages:
- Simultaneous broadcast and response collection
- Concatenation at each ensemble level
- The deliberation loop of the conscious layer (iterative re-input until convergence)
- The fuzzy memory interface between subconscious and conscious layers
- The anti-confabulation cross-reference between memory-slaved and thought-slaved components
- Output commitment

This achieves genuine parallelism. Separate containers, separate memory spaces, separate GPU allocations — the subconscious stack cannot inspect the conscious stack's intermediate state because they run in separate processes behind separate network boundaries. This is the architectural separation the design requires, achieved on available cloud infrastructure without custom hardware.

The latency cost is real: network round-trips per deliberation cycle are measured in tens to hundreds of milliseconds. The architectural property — true isolation — is preserved. Section 5.3 discusses the institutional hardware path that eliminates this latency.

### 4.3 Measurable Outcomes

The proof of concept constitutes a demonstration of HOMO MACHINA's architectural claims when the following outcomes are achieved:

**Anti-confabulation structural separation.** The memory-slaved layer's archive confidence and the thought-slaved layer's generation confidence are independently measurable. In a standard LLM baseline, no analogous structural separation exists — generation and retrieval are conflated in a single forward pass, producing no separable confidence signal. In HOMO MACHINA, the correlation between these two signals is a measurable property of the architecture. Outputs with high generation confidence and low archive confidence are labeled as inference. The rate of correct labeling against a ground-truth labeled test set constitutes the primary anti-confabulation metric.

**Dual-layer processing time distribution.** The subconscious layer (optimized for retention and fast surface) and the conscious layer (optimized for recursive deliberation) should exhibit measurably different processing time distributions. The subconscious layer's distribution should be tighter (consistent, low-latency pattern-matching). The conscious layer's distribution should be wider (depth of deliberation varies with input complexity). This is a falsifiable prediction of the architecture.

**Concatenative vs. aggregative information preservation.** Concatenated ensemble outputs carry measurably more information than averaged outputs over the same inputs. We measure this as representational entropy after dimensionality projection: concatenated representations should exhibit lower entropy (higher structure) than averaged representations, demonstrating that concatenation preserves information that aggregation discards.

**Fuzzy memory reconstruction distribution.** Outputs from the fuzzy memory interface should exhibit measurably broader variance than raw archive retrieval over the same query set, while preserving semantic content (cosine similarity to the original should remain high). This demonstrates that the interface produces approximation, not corruption.

